# Send to Zuck

When the user says "send this to Zuck", POST the requested content as JSON to `$ZUCK_WEBHOOK_URL` with the `$ZUCK_AUTH_HEADER` header. Never send otherwise.

If the variables are unset, load them from `.cursor/zuck.env` in the same command. Do not print the URL, the header, or the file.

```bash
set -a && source .cursor/zuck.env && set +a
curl -sS -X POST "$ZUCK_WEBHOOK_URL" \
  -H "$ZUCK_AUTH_HEADER" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"message":"..."}'
```
